[Music]  it's hard to believe but Kingdom Hearts  3 is finally out this long-awaited  adventure has a lot going for it that'll  please fans while also potentially  attracting folks who may have avoided  the series and its myriad spin-offs over  the years regardless of your background  there are several tips you'll need to  know should you decide to embark on this  magical Disney filled adventure the tips  we've compiled will help prepare you for  the challenges that lie ahead in Kingdom  Hearts 3 for others they'll reinforce  and refresh your memory of the general  habits to follow around getting the most  out of its most well-established  mechanics we even included a fair amount  on some of the new things you'll  encounter without spoiling too many of  the surprises of course so let's get  onto it  [Music]  as you progress your party constantly  learns new abilities most of which you  have to activate manually take time to  jump into the abilities screen to  activate them so you don't miss out on  the useful perks they offer in some  instances you might even learn an  ability that's required to progress  further so don't neglect it just make  sure you're properly managing your  abilities and setting up the ones you're  more likely to use as each ability does  have a cost that takes up your overall  ap threshold  [Music]  we got this the more you all upon  enemies the more special tax you can use  during a fight you might not know it but  you can actually cycle through which  attacks you can activate by simply  pressing the trigger buttons make use of  this to open up your strategic options  in the fight reserving special tax for  moments where they matter  [Music]  once you're able to prepare meals with  Remy be sure to cook up one of each dish  type this allows you to eat a full  course in the cuisine menu which gives  you a temporary special ability bonus  along side a buff to your stats to  ensure you have enough to cook with  always scour the environment for  potential ingredients break open boxes  shatter lanterns or raid some leftover  Chinese takeout do whatever you got to  do  you can also buy ingredients at the  moogle shop and Sora Donald and Goofy  will even inform you whenever there's  ingredients around my bet we'll find  some ingredients around here hope we  find some ingredients around here  as long as you're paying attention you  should be well stocked before long check  up on the menu frequently too as more  recipes will unlock as you gather more  ingredients in addition if you keep  cooking Uncle Scrooge will give you  special item rewards for completing  dishes on the menu  [Music]  you can equip up to three key blades in  Kingdom Hearts 3 as you unlock more make  sure to mix and match to see which  combination works best for you or for  the enemy types you're fighting in a  particular world it's typically smart to  equip key blades with contrasting form  changes in order to give you more  options for example the favorite  deputies varied close-range attacks  mesh well with the projectiles of a  shooting star and this is more of a  personal preference but we recommend  always having the Kingdom key in your  loadout as it provides the best balance  of them all its form change second form  is also useful given its extended combo  that and if you're a classic Kingdom  Hearts fan it doesn't make sense being  without it always check in at the moogle  shop not only to purchase potions ethers  and equipment but also to upgrade your  key blades and synthesize materials you  need the proper materials to upgrade a  keyblade so make sure you're constantly  collecting enemy drops and scouring the  environment for treasure chests it's a  lot of effort but worth it to enhance  the magic strengths and abilities of  your weapon on the other hand  synthesizing materials is useful for a  variety of reasons while you can utilize  this feature to craft healing potions  and other power-ups you'll generally  want to use it to craft armor  accessories and valuable materials for  upgrading key blades if you lack the  money to purchase equipment there's  typically a lot of powerful pieces you  can synthesize that'll either close the  gap or help you specialize your stats  further the moogle shop frequently  accompanies save points for a good  reason  so make a habit of checking it to see if  you can upgrade Sora and company  [Music]  the moogle shop may have plenty of items  and accessories to synthesize but  there's several that aren't made  available to you unless you complete the  mughals photo challenges these mini  quests require you to take photographs  of specific locales and enemy types  check in every once in a while to see  what snapshots the moogle needs as  you're often rewarded with new synthesis  recipes upon completing them usually for  accessories that are far better than the  standard ones listed  [Music]  this should be a given but make sure  you're jumping into the item screen to  use all the boost items for your stats  you earn throughout your adventure these  allow you to enhance your party stats  further outside of simply leveling up or  enhancing their equipment we generally  recommend handing off all the AP once  the Soraa as he gets access to far more  abilities than Donald and Goofy while  all the rest you can divvy up based on  how you want to build up your party  stats of course avoid giving these  boosts to temporary party members for  obvious reasons oh I'll lucky annalen  you learn early on in your adventure  about lucky emblems which are Mickey  Mouse symbols that you're encouraged to  photograph with your gummy phone the  reward for photographing Lucky emblems  isn't made entirely clear at first but  know that doing so will net you the  secret ending if that entices you then  we encourage you to always be on the  lookout Sora Donald and Goofy often note  when the Lucky emblem is nearby so take  the time to investigate hey I think  that's a lucky emblem let's see they're  usually hidden behind objects on walls  or somewhere up above if you're  struggling be sure to check out our  in-depth lucky emblem video guide  we're not gonna lie Kingdom Hearts has a  wacky story that's sometimes difficult  to understand and if you're someone  who's missed out on a few of the  spin-offs over the years you might feel  lost at times playing Kingdom Hearts 3  luckily the game has story summary  videos that offer a crash course on  everything you need to know before  playing including details on the major  players conflicts and history access  these videos from the memory archive  option in the main menu  we highly recommend giving them a look  so that you understand Kingdom Hearts as  story beats and characters better  if you're a longtime fan of Kingdom  Hearts you'll want to partake in the  battle gate mode that unlocks towards  the end of the game it's an optional  mode where you can take on difficult  combat challenges each has a star  difficulty rating ranging from 1 to 3  and can be pretty tough but we recommend  doing these challenges as completing  them earns you special reports much like  the ansan reports from the first two  Kingdom Hearts games that flesh out the  story further in addition you get new  selfie poses so if that doesn't entice  you then we don't know what will and  that's all the tips we've got if you've  got any that we didn't discuss here be  sure to leave them in the comments below  thanks for watching  you

